Z||000000||Gasolene||07-16-2001||05:15 PM||||everytime I drive over a speed bump, or any jerky motion, the engine shuts<BR>off for about 1/10 of a second.  I think there is a loose wire around the<BR>computer causing the spark plugs to stop for a split second.<P>How do I find the problem, there is tons of wire's and harnesses?<BR>or is this a ECM computer problem?<P>Gasolene@hotmail.com<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||07-16-2001||05:48 PM||||not sure of what car your talking about.but in any event I guess you need to start your carand start moving the wires around by hand near your computer esecially if thats where you think the problem is,then proceed to other areas. there really is no easy solution to electrical problems it is just a loy of detective work but yours seems easy enough to diaognois.when you post give a little more info like what kind of car motor etc.and how fast are you going over speed bumps let us know if this helps ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gasolene||07-16-2001||07:37 PM||||84 Fiero 2M4<BR>4cyl standard<P>doesn't really matter wat speed I'm goin.  and it doesn't always happen.  sometimes If I jerk the car sideways or turn sharp it happens.  Other times if I hit a pot hole in the road.<BR>To test the car, I put it in 1st gear and started pumping the gass to get the car to jerk around and this also produced the engine hesitation.||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||07-16-2001||08:40 PM||||Gasolene, I had same problem w/ my 84. One of the wires at the coil had broken in the insulation right at the terminal. They kinda hang off the coil and I guess broke one strand at a time over time. Usually made contact till a bump. I found it just as the above suggestion, start the car and gently move em around. Good luck<BR>Don & Jane<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 2.5<BR>not slow not fast-just halfast||||reg||1
Z||000004||DecadenceR||07-16-2001||09:51 PM||||I had the same problem as well, and it turned out to be a ground wire. I jst isconnected all grounds, cleaned up the contacts, and made sure I tightened them up really good. No problem since.||||reg||1
